1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,461
The pharmacy closed ten years ago.

2
00:00:02,461 --> 00:00:04,600
Tonight, its lights came back on.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:12,590
This is Afterhours: The Tenth Prescription, a pixel art
horror game about the people a place refuses to forget.

4
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:15,115
You are the last pharmacist on the night shift.

5
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:18,865
Somewhere beneath the counter are thirty missing names.

6
00:00:18,865 --> 00:00:23,492
Recover them, ward by ward, before the Unnamed find you.

7
00:00:23,492 --> 00:00:28,530
Your scanner reveals sealed records and briefly stops
nearby shadows.

8
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:33,041
But every pulse costs charge, and the sound brings others
closer.

9
00:00:33,041 --> 00:00:38,994
Walking quietly, breaking their line of sight, and knowing
when to hide can save your shift.

10
00:00:38,994 --> 00:00:42,615
Recovering a name takes a moment of stillness.

11
00:00:42,615 --> 00:00:47,719
That small pause becomes a difficult choice when something
is moving in the dark.

12
00:00:47,719 --> 00:00:53,891
Ten wards take you from a frozen dispensary to a flooded
archive and the final prescription.

13
00:00:53,891 --> 00:00:57,384
Each carries a different fragment of your sister's story.

14
00:00:57,384 --> 00:00:58,608
Follow the sound.

15
00:00:58,608 --> 00:00:59,845
Keep the names.

16
00:00:59,845 --> 00:01:02,680
Decide what the pharmacy should remember.

17
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:04,690
Play Afterhours in your browser.

18
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:06,791
Your shift begins at midnight.
